WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.370
- This was the only
kingdom in all of Africa

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.176
where women had an equal voice.

00:00:04.176 --> 00:00:06.926
(suspense music)

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:12.660
(bright upbeat music)

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.550
We are set in an actual historical world

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.117
yet some of our storytelling
is fictionalized.

00:00:19.117 --> 00:00:22.260
"Braveheart" was a template
absolutely for the film,

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.090
one of my favorite
movies, historical fiction

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.370
I think is really the best description.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.570
So many of the elements are
true and that was the fun part

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.470
to be authentic to everything
from who these women were,

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.540
the kingdom, what was
happening at that time,

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.610
the production, design,
everything mirrored

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.720
what it really was.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.760
Historically what was going on at the time

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.950
in terms of the big battle
between the two kingdoms

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.980
and what was going on politically,
socially, economically.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.780
To do that type of world building

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.940
for a story like this was fun.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.120
Our characters within this real world

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.210
were fictionalized yet they
reflected these real women,

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.550
what they went through.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.320
(bright traditional music)

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.540
I used the phrase intimately epic

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.490
with every department head and certainly,

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.050
when I spoke with Danny Hernandez

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:10.080
who's our fight and stunt
coordinator, and also our actors,

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.270
it started with the
conversations with them

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.170
that the best action is story
driven and character driven.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:17.250
And the best way to do that

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.230
is to have performance within it.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.390
So you guys are gonna be
doing your own fighting

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.320
and your own stunts.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.090
And it's one thing to say that,

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.220
it's another to have actors embrace that.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.722
Every single one of 'em
wanted to do everything

00:01:28.722 --> 00:01:31.620
and kept doing it until
they got it perfectly.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.500
It took Danny to create a fighting style

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.160
that an audience could believe
women legit beating men

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.470
which is what really happened.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.670
How do you create that?

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:42.630
What does that look like?

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.100
A lot of people working together

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.200
but it started with the
desire of the actors

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.980
to do what I asked of them
which was you're doing it all.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.680
It's breaking it down into pieces.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.140
When this character's
fighting, what is it about?

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.390
Giving each vignette that we have

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.590
a beginning, middle and end.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.590
And that the knowledge
of seeds that we planted

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.530
throughout the film that leads
us to this big epic battle

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:07.020
that some of those seeds
are now paying off in this.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.600
So again, that it is
personal and character driven

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.100
and story driven,

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.389
that is not just random
violence or random fighting.

00:02:13.389 --> 00:02:15.600
It was making it bite size

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.683
so that it didn't feel
overwhelming in shooting it.

00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:20.730
(bright traditional music)

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.670
People do not, even in this
day and age, think of women

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:27.870
as warriors, as fighters,
as having heart and courage.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:31.230
These women in the 1800s
absolutely had that.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.260
They were the main fighting
force of this kingdom

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.990
and they trained for it and
they wanted to be there,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.520
they wanted to be fighters.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.690
They were athletes.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:43.260
And there was a beauty in their power

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.870
in how they trained in
their athletic bodies.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.100
They were praised for it.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.990
We see what happens in this day and age

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.390
and it is getting better slowly

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:52.950
but it's still not to where it should be.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.860
The more we can put women
up on screen to show

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.920
that we have an innate warrior,
to celebrate their fitness

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.780
and their athleticism and their skill.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.900
Again, these are not stunt
doubles doing that fighting,

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:06.880
this is these actors, these
women, Viola Davis did that.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.850
Thuso Mbedu did that.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.800
We can do that, these are not superheroes,

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:11.940
these were real women.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.190
I hope we can see, yes, this is possible.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.438
I can be that.

00:03:15.438 --> 00:03:18.330
(soft ominous music)

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.220
This was the only kingdom in all of Africa

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.870
where women had an equal voice.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:24.540
On the council, for every
man, there was a woman

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.940
who had the equal power
and voice in the kingdom.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.030
The fact that the Woman
King was a real position,

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.830
we didn't make up this cool name,

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.780
it really was called the Woman King

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.890
and this woman was elevated
to a position next to the king

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:39.540
and helped him guide the kingdom.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.760
We're not just putting
these badass women on screen

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.890
but we're telling a bigger story than that

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.410
of who these women were,
what the society was like.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.900
But also in the research,
I didn't realize how big

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.660
dance was to this culture as well.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.720
So not only did these
women train to fight 24/7,

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.390
they also created these
elaborate choreographed dances

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:00.030
that celebrated themselves,
got them ready for war.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.610
I loved that I was able
to bring that element

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:03.938
within this film as well.

00:04:03.938 --> 00:04:06.900
(soft ominous music)

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.700
The Oyo battle, absolutely.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:13.500
It is an epic battle, I studied
with Polly Morgan, our DP,

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.727
we studied "Braveheart", "Gladiator",

00:04:15.727 --> 00:04:19.170
"Last of the Mohicans", it
was absolutely this thing

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.540
that was looming at
the end of the schedule

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.270
but I put it there one, to
give the actors enough time

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:27.600
to train for those sequences.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.030
I needed our crew to be
a place where we were all

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:33.690
so comfortable with each
other, working at another level

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.840
before we got into that because
it was absolutely daunting

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.970
and we had 11 days to shoot it.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.880
It was intimidating but everybody,

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.220
we just had a plan and we
stuck through that plan

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:45.053
and we got it done.

00:04:45.053 --> 00:04:48.090
(bright upbeat music)

